{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"383536fcaa4e2c98","type":"text","text":"\n1. Client Inference - Simple LLM call to register clients metadata\n\t1. business context\n\t2. organization name, description.\n\t3. client metadata\n\t4. source metadata (should include source name for every source addition).\n2. Ontology Agent - \n\t 1. Concepts\n\t 2. Relations\n3. Source Inference  - \n\t 1. Pick the all table names (cleaned table names)\n\t 2. Pick the Knowledge context content\n\t 3. Pick the client metadata embedding. \n\t 4. Pick the business context information along with Industry type \n4. Table Inference - \n\t 1. Pick the column info\n\t\t  1. data types\n\t\t  2. sample values\n\t 2. Pick the source embedding\n\t 3. Pick the business context information along with Industry type \n\t 4. Pick the knowledge context content\n\t 5. Ontology - LLm call to query ontology + relations ( top k ) - Critique ? - test variable - test_concept_id\n\t 6. Table embedding - \n\t\t  1. Follow the pattern \n\t\t\t   1. Identity\n\t\t\t   2. Semantic\n\t\t\t   3. Tech Description\n\t 7. Registered to table metadata mongo. \n5. Column Inference - \n\t 1. Pick the column info\n\t\t  1. Sample values\n\t\t  2. Data types * Column batch. \n\t 2. Pick the table metadata\n\t\t  1. Name\n\t\t  2. Embedding\n\t 3. Pick the source name and description\n\t 4. Pick the business context and industry type\n\t 5. Pick the knowledge context.\n\t 6. Pick the Ontology concept\n\t 7. Update the \n\t\t  1. Description -\n\t\t\t   1. should contain name, data type, concise definition.\n\t\t\t  2. Embedding\n\t\t\t  3. Follow the pattern\n\t\t\t\t   1. Identity\n\t\t\t\t   2. Semantic\n\t\t\t\t   3. Tech description\n6. PK Inference\n\t 1. Pick the table info\n\t\t  1. name\n\t\t  2. embedding input\n\t 2. Pick the column info\n\t\t  1. name \n\t\t  2. embedding input\n\t\t  3. sample values\n\t\t  4. data type\n\t 3. Pick the Knowledge context if available - table level\n\t 4. Pick the business context and industry type\n\t 5. Pick the ontology concepts of entity type\n7. Fk Inference\n\t 1. Pick the keyword match\n\t 2. Pick the semantic match\n\t 3. Complete RAG flow \n\t 4. Ask LLM to be Critique\n8. PKRT Inference while doing FK inference\n9. Re infer table embedding and description\n\t 1. Pick the current table embedding \n\t 2. Pick the column info\n\t\t  1. Name\n\t\t  2. description\n\t 3. Pick the source info \n\t\t  1. Name\n\t\t  2. embedding\n\t 4. Pick the PKRT\n\t 5. Pick the FKRT\n\t 6. Pick the ontology concepts\n\t 7. Pick the ontology relations\n10. Re infer source metadata\n\t 1. Pick the current source embedding\n\t 2. Pick the table info\n\t\t  1. name\n\t\t  2. embedding input\n \n11. Edges Inference \n\t 1. Align with new schema\n\t 2. Pure python script\n\t 3. Enrich the table , column , source levels descriptions \n12. Binding - \n\t 1. Pick each table \n\t 2. Prepare a semantic query \n\t 3. Search in the Ontology concepts\n\t\t  1. Top K = 2\n\t\t  2. Ask LLM to pick one topmost with high confidence\n\t 4. Append the concept id to table metadata\n\t 5. variable name - concept_id","x":-440,"y":-2840,"width":780,"height":2400},
		{"id":"3ae0558afb7618dc","type":"text","text":"Table inference process:\n1. Make table name clean. \n\t1. source name, description\n\t2. table be_name, column names and sample values. \n2. ","x":971,"y":-2891,"width":589,"height":451},
